00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:57.000
When the other guests asked what happened, detectives described it as what it appeared to be. A natural causes thing. Given that Greg Flaniken was a middle-aged long-term smoker with no known illnesses or external injuries, the expectation was that his death had likely been caused by a major medical event, such as a cardiac arrest, stroke or aneurysm. When soon, Susie Flaniken was notified, the only consolation to her grief was that Greg would have likely wanted her this way. She later told Vanity Fair that Greg was a stubborn man who did an exercise, had no interest in fitness, and never went to the doctor. When hearing about people who died suddenly, he would make remarks such as, Lucky bastard, that's how I want to go.

