Greg's autopsy was carried out the following day by Dr. Tommy Brown, a rest of a rest of suspected Jefferson County Medical Examiner with a strong reputation among local law enforcement and the courts for being meticulous, consistent, and conservative in the way he reached conclusions. Dr. Brown began his standard external examination and noted there was a small abrasion on Greg's cheek, which was consistent with him having collapsed and struck the carpet. He then moved on to Greg's groin area and noticed there was a small vertical laceration on his scrotum, about half an inch long. At first glance, it was so small that it could have been mistaken for a superficial injury, but the tissue around it was markedly bruised and swollen, indicating it had been

