hit by something hard. Dr. Brown proceeded to the internal examination. To his surprise, he found that Greg's abdominal cavity contained a significant amount of blood. His liver was also lacerated and torn, His intestines were perforated in multiple places, his stomach showed bruising, and two of his ribs were fractured. There was also a hole in the right atrium of Greg's heart. Dr. Brown was taken aback. It looked to him like Greg had suffered some kind of extremely hard blow to the chest, but this type of extensive internal trauma was more commonly associated with high-impact

