00:09:27.000 --> 00:10:24.000
incidents such as a car crash or something heavy falling on a person, not a lone man relaxing in a hotel room. Although it went against the physical evidence at the scene, Dr Brown concluded that Greg Flanickens injuries were consistent with severe blunt force trauma and that he had likely been beaten to death or crushed. In the official documentation under manner of death, he wrote, homicide. When the autopsy findings arrived at the Beaumont Police Department, Detective Scott Apple was shocked. Having attended the relatively unremarkable scene at the MCM Elegante Hotel, the realization dawned on him that he now had a murder investigation on his hands. But if Greg Flaniken hadn't simply collapsed from a medical event, that left just two broad possibilities.

