Apple considered the possibility that something heavy could have fallen onto Greg, but nothing in the hotel room supported this theory. He also wondered whether Greg could have been assaulted in the hallway or another part of the hotel and then left for dead in his room. But there were no visible marks on the carpet that suggested Greg's body had been dragged and it seemed highly unlikely that someone could have moved an adult male through a public hotel without being seen or heard. And if Greg had indeed been the victim of a homicide, then there was a bigger question of who could have killed him and why. For Susie Flaniken, the possibility that someone might have wanted to harm her husband seemed preposterous. Greg was the love of her life.

