power had been restored, and the fatal injuries were inflicted sometime after Garcia left Room 348, around 8.30pm. Exactly when and how remained unknown. The Ardidge also drew attention to the room directly next door to Greg's, Room 349. At the time of Greg's death, a group of union electricians were staying at the hotel while working on a refinery expansion in Beaumont. It was a major project and many of the electricians had come from interstate to see it through. After work, in the evenings, they often gathered in one another's rooms to drink and socialise. Two of the electricians had been staying in room 349 and witnesses said that on the night of September 15, they and some others had been drinking in their room and getting a bit rowdy.

