before eventually admitting he'd come clean and told the police the truth. There was a long silence. Lance Mueller then asked Steinmetz if he'd told them about the gun going off. Steinmetz said yes. He told Mueller that the investigators believed Greg Flaniken had died from that gunshot. Mueller refused to accept it. He said his lawyer had obtained a copy of the autopsy report and there was no mention of a gunshot wound.

