but they did need to show that Mueller's conduct met the threshold of recklessness and that his actions had caused Greg's death. Having sought an opinion from another medical examiner, the prosecution's case was that Greg had been relaxed, on his bed when a bullet entered his scrotum, tearing upward into his body, lacerating organs and breaking bones, before lodging deep in his chest. The bullet wound had not been visible because it was hidden by folds of flesh, which resulted in the mark looking more like a bruise. In contrast to Dr. Brown, who believed it would have taken Greg anywhere between 30 seconds and

