removed the weapon and made no effort to check on Greg, or alert hotel staff or the police while Greg's death was still being treated as a medical event. The prosecution also pointed out that while on bail, Mueller had been arrested in Wisconsin for drunk driving. It was his fourth such offense, and given that alcohol had also been involved with the Greg Flaniken incident, the prosecution honed in on this hard. Lance Mueller ultimately entered a no-contest plea to manslaughter, which meant that he didn't didn't admit guilt, but didn't contest the charge either. By the time Mueller's sentencing hearing took place the following month, over two years had passed since Greg Flanagan's death. It had been

